# FPGA / Zynq agent rules (BitNet on Zybo)

Design reference: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Status: `STATUS.md`.

## Board and part

- Board: **Digilent Zybo Z7-10**, part `xc7z010clg400-1`, board part `digilentinc.com:zybo-z7-10:part0:1.2`
- Tool, board-file and model paths: `local.mk` / `SETUP.md` (defaults `D:\Xilinx`, `D:\xilinx-tools`).
- Power: on USB power run the engine at 83-100 MHz (brownout above ~3.2 GB/s); 142.9 MHz needs the 5 V barrel supply.

## Toolchain

- Vivado/Vitis **2026.1** in `D:\Xilinx`. Source `tools/setup/env.ps1` before every Vivado command in a new shell.
- **Never use `xsct`** on 2026.x; use the Vitis **Python API** and **XSDB** (`tools/setup/run_ps_xsdb.ps1`).

## Build discipline

- Simulate (`make sim`, Vivado xsim) before synthesis whenever RTL changes.
- Scripts over GUI; never commit generated Vivado/Vitis output (`build/` is ignored).
- `tools/bitnet/engine.py` is the golden model for every layer output.
- Engine weight format (v3): T5, five ternary weights per byte in base 3, 40 per 64-bit beat, row-major (`tools/bitnet/engine_format.py`).

## Hardware safety

- `make check-ftdi` must pass before any JTAG access (mismatched FTDI drivers bluescreened this PC).
- If the board is unresponsive after **one** software reset, stop and ask the user to power-cycle.
